WEBVTT

NOTE The Rogue Render, the approved 50-second cut (sha256 c7a31330), made in Media OS. Captions for the studio's player, off until a viewer turns them on.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
[Stately strings]

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:02.300
[A digital glitch]

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.500
[Playful plucked strings]

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:03.700
[Strings crash, klaxons blare]

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.395
[Director, whispering] It changed the ad...

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.225
[Director, whispering] It's shipping the crustacean.

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.828
[Director, shouting] Dear God, who approved the lobster?!

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.560
[Narrator] When nobody has to say yes...

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.000
[Sparks crackle]

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:16.500
[The power cuts out]

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.480
[Narrator] ...the lobster goes live.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:20.500
[Everything winds down to a stop]

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.900
[Silence]

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.000
[A heavy thud]

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.270
[Narrator] Imprimatur holds the release until a person approves it,

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.000
[A tiny click]

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:32.950
[A huge clunk]

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.320
[Narrator] and records the time and exactly which file was approved.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.000
[The stately strings return]

00:00:40.125 --> 00:00:40.750
[Glasses clink]

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.890
[Narrator] Imprimatur. Ask to see it run.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.000
[A single pluck]

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.500
[The strings close, softly]
